---
title: ACP-Compatible Harness
id: acp-compatible-harness
description: "Plug any Agent Client Protocol (ACP) coding agent into a TanStack AI sandbox with one generic harness adapter — no dedicated package required."
keywords:
  - tanstack ai
  - acp
  - agent client protocol
  - coding agent
  - harness
  - sandbox
  - custom adapter
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Coding-agent CLIs that speak the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://agentclientprotocol.com","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Agent Client Protocol"}]},{"type":"text","value":" (ACP) — "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grok"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gemini --acp"},{"type":"text","value":", and others — expose a long-lived JSON-RPC session you can drive from a sandbox. Instead of a dedicated package per agent, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"acpCompatible"},{"type":"text","value":" builds a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" adapter for "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"any"}]},{"type":"text","value":" ACP-compliant CLI: configure how to launch it once, select a model per call, and pass it into a sandbox."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"It is the harness equivalent of the "},{"type":"link","href":"./openai-compatible","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenAI-Compatible adapter"}]},{"type":"text","value":". Use it when your agent speaks ACP but has no "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-*"},{"type":"text","value":" package. If a dedicated harness adapter exists ("},{"type":"link","href":"./grok-build","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Grok Build"}]},{"type":"text","value":", and others), prefer it — those carry curated per-model metadata and vendor-specific behavior."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"authentication","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Authentication"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The default "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"authMode"},{"type":"text","value":" is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'api-key'"},{"type":"text","value":". Set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'host'"},{"type":"text","value":" when the agent should use\na CLI login on the machine. The sandbox type does not pick this. See\n"},{"type":"link","href":"../sandbox/auth","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Harness Auth"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { acpCompatibleText } from \"@tanstack/ai-acp\"\n\nacpCompatibleText(\"composer-2.5\", {\n  name: \"acp\",\n  command: ({ model }) => `grok agent -m '${model}' --always-approve stdio`,\n  authMethodId: \"xai.api_key\",\n})\n\nacpCompatibleText(\"composer-2.5\", {\n  name: \"acp\",\n  command: ({ model }) => `grok agent -m '${model}' --always-approve stdio`,\n  authMode: \"host\",\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'api-key'"},{"type":"text","value":" (default): call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"authenticate"},{"type":"text","value":" with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"authMethodId"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'host'"},{"type":"text","value":": skip ACP "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"authenticate"},{"type":"text","value":". Use the CLI login on the machine."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"outputSchema"},{"type":"text","value":" on the same "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" call. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"acpCompatible"},{"type":"text","value":" adds the schema to the prompt and parses the last assistant text. Native harness tools still run on that turn. Read the typed object from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"await chat()"},{"type":"text","value":", from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useChat().final"},{"type":"text","value":", or from the assistant "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"structured-output"},{"type":"text","value":" part. See "},{"type":"link","href":"../structured-outputs/harnesses","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Harness Agents"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"installation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Installation"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"acpCompatible"},{"type":"text","value":" ships in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-acp"},{"type":"text","value":". You drive it inside a sandbox, so install the sandbox package and a provider too:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"package-manager","mode":"install"},"children":[],"properties":{"data-package-manager-meta":"{\"packagesByFramework\":{\"react\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-acp\",\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-sandbox\",\"@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\"]],\"vue\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-acp\",\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-sandbox\",\"@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\"]],\"solid\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-acp\",\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-sandbox\",\"@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\"]],\"svelte\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-acp\",\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-sandbox\",\"@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\"]],\"preact\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-acp\",\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-sandbox\",\"@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\"]],\"angular\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-acp\",\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-sandbox\",\"@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\"]],\"vanilla\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-acp\",\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-sandbox\",\"@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\"]],\"octane\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-acp\",\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-sandbox\",\"@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\"]]},\"mode\":\"install\"}"}},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"basic-usage","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Basic Usage"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Configure the harness once with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"acpCompatible({ name, command })"},{"type":"text","value":", then select a model per call. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"command"},{"type":"text","value":" builds the shell command that launches the agent's ACP server over "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"stdio"}]},{"type":"text","value":" inside the sandbox:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { acpCompatible } from '@tanstack/ai-acp'\nimport {\n  createSecrets,\n  defineSandbox,\n  defineWorkspace,\n  githubRepo,\n  withSandbox,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { dockerSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker'\nimport { messages } from './chat-context'\n\n// Configure the \"pi\" agent harness once:\nconst pi = acpCompatible({\n  name: 'pi',\n  command: ({ model, harnessCwd }) => `pi --acp -m ${model} --cwd ${harnessCwd}`,\n  authMethodId: 'pi-api-key', // when the harness advertises an ACP auth method\n  refusalMessage: 'Pi refused the request.',\n})\n\nconst sandbox = defineSandbox({\n  id: 'pi-agent',\n  provider: dockerSandbox({ image: 'node:22' }),\n  workspace: defineWorkspace({\n    source: githubRepo({ repo: 'owner/app' }),\n    setup: ['npm install -g pi-cli'], // install the agent CLI into the image\n    secrets: createSecrets({ PI_API_KEY: process.env.PI_API_KEY ?? '' }),\n  }),\n})\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: pi('pi-fast'),\n  messages,\n  middleware: [withSandbox(sandbox)],\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You get the full ACP flow for free: sandbox resolution, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":"-tool → MCP bridging, session resume, permission handling, abort, and AG-UI event translation."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"one-shot-usage","children":[{"type":"text","value":"One-Shot Usage"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For a single model, skip the harness-factory and build the adapter inline with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"acpCompatibleText"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { acpCompatibleText } from '@tanstack/ai-acp'\nimport { withSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { sandbox } from './sandbox'\nimport { messages } from './chat-context'\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: acpCompatibleText('pi-fast', {\n    name: 'pi',\n    command: ({ model }) => `pi --acp -m ${model}`,\n  }),\n  messages,\n  middleware: [withSandbox(sandbox)],\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"typed-output","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Typed output"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"outputSchema"},{"type":"text","value":" on the same "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" call. The agent runs its native tools. Then the adapter parses the last assistant text as JSON."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { acpCompatibleText } from '@tanstack/ai-acp'\nimport { withSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\nimport { sandbox } from './sandbox'\nimport { messages } from './chat-context'\n\nconst ReportSchema = z.object({\n  name: z.string(),\n  oneLiner: z.string(),\n})\n\nexport async function POST() {\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: acpCompatibleText('pi-fast', {\n      name: 'pi',\n      command: ({ model }) => `pi --acp -m ${model}`,\n    }),\n    messages,\n    outputSchema: ReportSchema,\n    stream: true,\n    middleware: [withSandbox(sandbox)],\n  })\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On the client, walk "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"messages[].parts"},{"type":"text","value":" for tool calls and reasoning. Read the typed object from the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"structured-output"},{"type":"text","value":" part or from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useChat().final"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst ReportSchema = z.object({\n  name: z.string(),\n  oneLiner: z.string(),\n})\n\nfunction Report() {\n  const { messages, final } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/report'),\n    outputSchema: ReportSchema,\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <>\n      {messages.map((message) =>\n        message.parts.map((part, index) => {\n          if (part.type === 'tool-call') {\n            return <p key={part.id}>{part.name}</p>\n          }\n          if (part.type === 'structured-output') {\n            const report = part.data ?? part.partial\n            return report?.name ? <h2 key={index}>{report.name}</h2> : null\n          }\n          return null\n        }),\n      )}\n      {final ? <p>{final.oneLiner}</p> : null}\n    </>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See "},{"type":"link","href":"../structured-outputs/harnesses","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Harness Agents"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for the full part list and the repo-report example."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"typed-models-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Typed models & options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Like "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openaiCompatible"},{"type":"text","value":", you can declare the harness's "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"models"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and its\nper-call "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"options"}]},{"type":"text","value":" so the whole thing is type-checked. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"models"},{"type":"text","value":" constrains the\nfactory's argument; "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" is a type-only brand ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{} as { … }"},{"type":"text","value":", unused at\nruntime) describing what "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat({ modelOptions })"},{"type":"text","value":" accepts. Declared options are\nmerged with the base ACP options and handed to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"command"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openTransport"},{"type":"text","value":" as\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.modelOptions"},{"type":"text","value":", so you can turn them into CLI flags:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { acpCompatible } from '@tanstack/ai-acp'\n\nconst pi = acpCompatible({\n  name: 'pi',\n  models: ['pi-fast', 'pi-pro'],\n  modelOptions: {} as { reasoningEffort?: 'low' | 'high' },\n  command: ({ model, harnessCwd, modelOptions }) =>\n    `pi --acp -m ${model} --cwd ${harnessCwd}` +\n    (modelOptions?.reasoningEffort ? ` --effort ${modelOptions.reasoningEffort}` : ''),\n})\n\npi('pi-pro') // ok\n// pi('pi-ultra') // type error — not in `models`","lang":"ts"},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { withSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { pi } from './pi-harness'\nimport { sandbox } from './sandbox'\nimport { messages } from './chat-context'\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: pi('pi-pro'),\n  modelOptions: { reasoningEffort: 'high' }, // typed against the declared options\n  messages,\n  middleware: [withSandbox(sandbox)],\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The base options are always available on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" regardless of what you\ndeclare: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sessionId"},{"type":"text","value":" (resume), "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cwd"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"authMode"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"authMethodId"},{"type":"text","value":", and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"permissionMode"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"configuration","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Configuration"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Field"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Purpose"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"name"},{"type":"text","value":" (required)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Harness label, log prefix, and the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<name>.session-id"},{"type":"text","value":" CUSTOM event name."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"models"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The model ids this harness accepts — declaring them makes "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"harness('id')"},{"type":"text","value":" type-safe (unknown ids are rejected). Omit to accept any string."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type-only brand for the per-call options accepted via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat({ modelOptions })"},{"type":"text","value":". Declare with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{} as { … }"},{"type":"text","value":"; merged with the base options and exposed on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.modelOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"command"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openTransport"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"command"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Build the "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"stdio"}]},{"type":"text","value":" launch command from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ model, cwd, harnessCwd, sandbox, env, modelOptions, signal }"},{"type":"text","value":". Required unless "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openTransport"},{"type":"text","value":" is given."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"skillsDir"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The harness's skills directory (relative to the workspace root, e.g. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'.pi/skills'"},{"type":"text","value":") — its native convention, like Claude Code's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".claude/skills"},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withSandbox"},{"type":"text","value":" workspace "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gitSkill"},{"type":"text","value":"s are linked here. Omit and gitSkills are left unlinked (warned)."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openTransport"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Open any "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AcpSessionTransport"},{"type":"text","value":" yourself (e.g. boot a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"serve"},{"type":"text","value":" process and connect over WebSocket). Overrides "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"command"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cwd"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Working directory inside the sandbox (default "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/workspace"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"env"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Extra environment variables for the harness process."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"authMode"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'api-key'"},{"type":"text","value":" (default) uses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"authMethodId"},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'host'"},{"type":"text","value":" skips ACP "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"authenticate"},{"type":"text","value":". See "},{"type":"link","href":"../sandbox/auth","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Harness Auth"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"authMethodId"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ACP auth method to select before the session starts. Ignored when "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"authMode"},{"type":"text","value":" is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'host'"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"permissionMode"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'default'"},{"type":"text","value":" | "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'acceptEdits'"},{"type":"text","value":" | "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'bypassPermissions'"},{"type":"text","value":" (default)."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"permissions"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'headless'"},{"type":"text","value":" (auto-resolve, default) or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'interactive'"},{"type":"text","value":" (emit approval-requested events for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ask"},{"type":"text","value":" prompts)."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onPermissionRequest"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom permission handler; overrides "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"permissions"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"permissionMode"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"refusalMessage"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RUN_ERROR"},{"type":"text","value":" message when the harness refuses a request."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"planEventName"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Emit ACP "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"plan"},{"type":"text","value":" updates as a CUSTOM event under this name."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"emitDiff"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Emit the post-run "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"git diff"},{"type":"text","value":" of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cwd"},{"type":"text","value":" as a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"file.changed"},{"type":"text","value":" CUSTOM event (off by default)."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onExtNotification"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Handle vendor "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"_x/…"},{"type":"text","value":" JSON-RPC notifications."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"buildPrompt"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Override how chat history maps to the harness prompt."}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"websocket-and-custom-transports","children":[{"type":"text","value":"WebSocket and Custom Transports"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Some harnesses run an ACP server you reach over WebSocket rather than stdio (the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grok agent serve"},{"type":"text","value":" pattern). Open the transport yourself with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openTransport"},{"type":"text","value":" — it receives the same context and returns an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AcpSessionTransport"},{"type":"text","value":". Put all teardown in the returned transport's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dispose"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { acpCompatible, startAcpServerInSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-acp'\n\nconst myAgent = acpCompatible({\n  name: 'my-agent',\n  openTransport: async ({ sandbox, model, harnessCwd, signal }) => {\n    const server = await startAcpServerInSandbox(sandbox, {\n      port: 9100,\n      cwd: harnessCwd,\n      command: `my-agent serve --bind 0.0.0.0:9100 -m ${model}`,\n      readyMarker: 'listening',\n      buildWsUrl: ({ channel, port }) =>\n        `${channel.url.replace(/^http/i, 'ws')}:${port}`,\n      ...(signal ? { signal } : {}),\n    })\n    const ws = await server.connect(signal)\n    return {\n      kind: 'stream',\n      stream: ws.stream,\n      dispose: async () => {\n        ws.close()\n        await server.dispose()\n      },\n    }\n  },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"permissions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Permissions"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Inside a sandbox the sandbox itself is the security boundary, so the default "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'headless'"},{"type":"text","value":" strategy with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"permissionMode: 'bypassPermissions'"},{"type":"text","value":" lets the agent edit files and run commands without prompting. To surface tool approvals to a client instead, switch to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'interactive'"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { acpCompatible } from '@tanstack/ai-acp'\n\nconst pi = acpCompatible({\n  name: 'pi',\n  command: ({ model }) => `pi --acp -m ${model}`,\n  permissions: 'interactive', // emit approval-requested events for `ask` prompts\n  permissionMode: 'acceptEdits', // still auto-approve file edits\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":"-provided tools bridged into the agent are always auto-approved, regardless of mode."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"session-resume","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Session Resume"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On every run the adapter emits the harness session id as a CUSTOM event named "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<name>.session-id"},{"type":"text","value":" (e.g. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pi.session-id"},{"type":"text","value":"). Thread that id back through "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions.sessionId"},{"type":"text","value":" on the next call and the harness resumes the session — only the trailing user message is sent, since the agent already holds the prior context:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat, chatParamsFromRequest, toServerSentEventsResponse } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { withSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { pi } from './pi-harness' // the configured `acpCompatible(...)` factory\nimport { sandbox } from './sandbox'\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const params = await chatParamsFromRequest(request)\n  const sessionId =\n    typeof params.forwardedProps.sessionId === 'string'\n      ? params.forwardedProps.sessionId\n      : undefined\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: pi('pi-fast'),\n    messages: params.messages,\n    middleware: [withSandbox(sandbox)],\n    modelOptions: { sessionId },\n  })\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"workspace-skills","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Workspace skills"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When you provision a "},{"type":"link","href":"../sandbox/workspace","children":[{"type":"text","value":"workspace"}]},{"type":"text","value":" via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withSandbox"},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"acpCompatible"},{"type":"text","value":" projects its skills into the harness — each kind lands where that\nharness expects it:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Workspace input"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"How "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"acpCompatible"},{"type":"text","value":" projects it"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mcpSkill(name, config)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Passed to the agent over "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ACP natively"}]},{"type":"text","value":" via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"newSession"},{"type":"text","value":"'s "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mcpServers"},{"type":"text","value":" (secrets/bearer headers resolved). No config file — that's the ACP advantage over file-based harnesses."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gitSkill({ repo })"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cloned during bootstrap, then linked into your declared "},{"type":"link","href":"#configuration","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"skillsDir"}]},{"type":"text","value":" (e.g. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".pi/skills"},{"type":"text","value":"). Omit "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"skillsDir"},{"type":"text","value":" and it's left unlinked (with a warning)."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fileSkill({ path, content })"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Written into the workspace root during bootstrap (provider-agnostic)."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"instructions"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Written to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AGENTS.md"},{"type":"text","value":" (and symlinks) during bootstrap."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"agentSkill(name)"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"plugins"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No generic ACP primitive — warned and skipped. Provide a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gitSkill"},{"type":"text","value":" or MCP server instead."}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"secrets"},{"type":"text","value":" declared on the workspace are injected into the agent's environment at\ncreate/resume (never persisted to snapshots), so the harness CLI picks them up\nlike any env var."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"protocol-coverage","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Protocol coverage"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"acpCompatible"},{"type":"text","value":" implements the "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"client / orchestration"}]},{"type":"text","value":" side of ACP — enough to\ndrive an agent through a full prompt turn, not the entire protocol surface. It is\na compliant "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"minimal"}]},{"type":"text","value":" client: everything it doesn't implement is either\ncapability-gated (so advertising non-support is the spec-defined behavior) or a\nrendering choice, never a violation."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Covered:"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialize"},{"type":"text","value":" handshake — sends "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"clientInfo"},{"type":"text","value":" + the protocol version, negotiates the version, advertises capabilities."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"authenticate"},{"type":"text","value":" (when the agent advertises auth methods), "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"session/new"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"session/load"},{"type":"text","value":" (resume), "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"session/prompt"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"session/cancel"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"session/request_permission"},{"type":"text","value":" with all four option kinds, mapped by "},{"type":"link","href":"#permissions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"permission mode"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"All streamed "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"session/update"},{"type":"text","value":"s that carry turn output: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"agent_message_chunk"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"agent_thought_chunk"},{"type":"text","value":" (→ reasoning), "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tool_call"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tool_call_update"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"plan"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"All five stop reasons ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"end_turn"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"max_tokens"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"max_turn_requests"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"refusal"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cancelled"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Surfaced as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CUSTOM"},{"type":"text","value":" stream events"}]},{"type":"text","value":" (the AG-UI chat-event protocol has no\nfirst-class event for non-text assistant output, so these ride on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CUSTOM"},{"type":"text","value":"):"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<name>.session-id"},{"type":"text","value":" — the harness session id, for "},{"type":"link","href":"#session-resume","children":[{"type":"text","value":"resume"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<name>.message-content"},{"type":"text","value":" — non-text agent content ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"image"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"audio"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resource"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resource_link"},{"type":"text","value":" blocks). Its "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"value"},{"type":"text","value":" is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ content: <ACP content block> }"},{"type":"text","value":". Non-text "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"tool"}]},{"type":"text","value":" content (diffs, terminal, images) is preserved inside the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TOOL_CALL_RESULT"},{"type":"text","value":" payload."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"the plan event, when you set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"planEventName"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Not implemented (by design):"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fs/read_text_file"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fs/write_text_file"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"terminal/*"},{"type":"text","value":" — advertised as unsupported. The agent runs inside the sandbox with direct filesystem and shell access, so it never delegates these back to the client."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sending "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"multimodal prompts"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — prompts are sent as text. (Agent multimodal "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"output"}]},{"type":"text","value":" is surfaced via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"message-content"},{"type":"text","value":" above.)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Incremental "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"usage_update"},{"type":"text","value":" (final turn usage is reported instead), "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"available_commands_update"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"current_mode_update"},{"type":"text","value":", and experimental features (elicitation, NES, providers, session modes/config)."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"next-steps","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Next Steps"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../sandbox/overview","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sandbox Overview"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — how harnesses run inside a sandbox"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./grok-build","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Grok Build Adapter"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — a first-class ACP harness adapter"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../sandbox/tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sandbox Tools"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — bridge your app's tools into the agent"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./openai-compatible","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenAI-Compatible Adapter"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — the same idea for model providers"}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"authentication","text":"Authentication","level":2},{"id":"installation","text":"Installation","level":2},{"id":"basic-usage","text":"Basic Usage","level":2},{"id":"one-shot-usage","text":"One-Shot Usage","level":2},{"id":"typed-output","text":"Typed output","level":2},{"id":"typed-models-options","text":"Typed models & options","level":2},{"id":"configuration","text":"Configuration","level":2},{"id":"websocket-and-custom-transports","text":"WebSocket and Custom Transports","level":2},{"id":"permissions","text":"Permissions","level":2},{"id":"session-resume","text":"Session Resume","level":2},{"id":"workspace-skills","text":"Workspace skills","level":2},{"id":"protocol-coverage","text":"Protocol coverage","level":2},{"id":"next-steps","text":"Next Steps","level":2}]},"frameworks":["react","vue","solid","svelte","preact","angular","vanilla","octane"],"downloadMarkdown":"\nCoding-agent CLIs that speak the [Agent Client Protocol](https://agentclientprotocol.com) (ACP) — `grok`, `gemini --acp`, and others — expose a long-lived JSON-RPC session you can drive from a sandbox. Instead of a dedicated package per agent, `acpCompatible` builds a `chat()` adapter for **any** ACP-compliant CLI: configure how to launch it once, select a model per call, and pass it into a sandbox.\n\nIt is the harness equivalent of the [OpenAI-Compatible adapter](./openai-compatible). Use it when your agent speaks ACP but has no `@tanstack/ai-*` package. If a dedicated harness adapter exists ([Grok Build](./grok-build), and others), prefer it — those carry curated per-model metadata and vendor-specific behavior.\n\n## Authentication\n\nThe default `authMode` is `'api-key'`. Set `'host'` when the agent should use\na CLI login on the machine. The sandbox type does not pick this. See\n[Harness Auth](../sandbox/auth).\n\n```ts\nimport { acpCompatibleText } from \"@tanstack/ai-acp\"\n\nacpCompatibleText(\"composer-2.5\", {\n  name: \"acp\",\n  command: ({ model }) => `grok agent -m '${model}' --always-approve stdio`,\n  authMethodId: \"xai.api_key\",\n})\n\nacpCompatibleText(\"composer-2.5\", {\n  name: \"acp\",\n  command: ({ model }) => `grok agent -m '${model}' --always-approve stdio`,\n  authMode: \"host\",\n})\n```\n\n- `'api-key'` (default): call `authenticate` with `authMethodId`.\n- `'host'`: skip ACP `authenticate`. Use the CLI login on the machine.\n\nPass `outputSchema` on the same `chat()` call. `acpCompatible` adds the schema to the prompt and parses the last assistant text. Native harness tools still run on that turn. Read the typed object from `await chat()`, from `useChat().final`, or from the assistant `structured-output` part. See [Harness Agents](../structured-outputs/harnesses).\n\n## Installation\n\n`acpCompatible` ships in `@tanstack/ai-acp`. You drive it inside a sandbox, so install the sandbox package and a provider too:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai-acp @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-sandbox @tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\nvue: @tanstack/ai-acp @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-sandbox @tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\nsolid: @tanstack/ai-acp @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-sandbox @tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai-acp @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-sandbox @tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\npreact: @tanstack/ai-acp @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-sandbox @tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\nangular: @tanstack/ai-acp @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-sandbox @tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai-acp @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-sandbox @tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\noctane: @tanstack/ai-acp @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-sandbox @tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n## Basic Usage\n\nConfigure the harness once with `acpCompatible({ name, command })`, then select a model per call. `command` builds the shell command that launches the agent's ACP server over **stdio** inside the sandbox:\n\n```ts\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { acpCompatible } from '@tanstack/ai-acp'\nimport {\n  createSecrets,\n  defineSandbox,\n  defineWorkspace,\n  githubRepo,\n  withSandbox,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { dockerSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker'\nimport { messages } from './chat-context'\n\n// Configure the \"pi\" agent harness once:\nconst pi = acpCompatible({\n  name: 'pi',\n  command: ({ model, harnessCwd }) => `pi --acp -m ${model} --cwd ${harnessCwd}`,\n  authMethodId: 'pi-api-key', // when the harness advertises an ACP auth method\n  refusalMessage: 'Pi refused the request.',\n})\n\nconst sandbox = defineSandbox({\n  id: 'pi-agent',\n  provider: dockerSandbox({ image: 'node:22' }),\n  workspace: defineWorkspace({\n    source: githubRepo({ repo: 'owner/app' }),\n    setup: ['npm install -g pi-cli'], // install the agent CLI into the image\n    secrets: createSecrets({ PI_API_KEY: process.env.PI_API_KEY ?? '' }),\n  }),\n})\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: pi('pi-fast'),\n  messages,\n  middleware: [withSandbox(sandbox)],\n})\n```\n\nYou get the full ACP flow for free: sandbox resolution, `chat()`-tool → MCP bridging, session resume, permission handling, abort, and AG-UI event translation.\n\n## One-Shot Usage\n\nFor a single model, skip the harness-factory and build the adapter inline with `acpCompatibleText`:\n\n```ts\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { acpCompatibleText } from '@tanstack/ai-acp'\nimport { withSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { sandbox } from './sandbox'\nimport { messages } from './chat-context'\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: acpCompatibleText('pi-fast', {\n    name: 'pi',\n    command: ({ model }) => `pi --acp -m ${model}`,\n  }),\n  messages,\n  middleware: [withSandbox(sandbox)],\n})\n```\n\n## Typed output\n\nPass `outputSchema` on the same `chat()` call. The agent runs its native tools. Then the adapter parses the last assistant text as JSON.\n\n```ts\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { acpCompatibleText } from '@tanstack/ai-acp'\nimport { withSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\nimport { sandbox } from './sandbox'\nimport { messages } from './chat-context'\n\nconst ReportSchema = z.object({\n  name: z.string(),\n  oneLiner: z.string(),\n})\n\nexport async function POST() {\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: acpCompatibleText('pi-fast', {\n      name: 'pi',\n      command: ({ model }) => `pi --acp -m ${model}`,\n    }),\n    messages,\n    outputSchema: ReportSchema,\n    stream: true,\n    middleware: [withSandbox(sandbox)],\n  })\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}\n```\n\nOn the client, walk `messages[].parts` for tool calls and reasoning. Read the typed object from the `structured-output` part or from `useChat().final`.\n\n```tsx\nimport { useChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst ReportSchema = z.object({\n  name: z.string(),\n  oneLiner: z.string(),\n})\n\nfunction Report() {\n  const { messages, final } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/report'),\n    outputSchema: ReportSchema,\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <>\n      {messages.map((message) =>\n        message.parts.map((part, index) => {\n          if (part.type === 'tool-call') {\n            return <p key={part.id}>{part.name}</p>\n          }\n          if (part.type === 'structured-output') {\n            const report = part.data ?? part.partial\n            return report?.name ? <h2 key={index}>{report.name}</h2> : null\n          }\n          return null\n        }),\n      )}\n      {final ? <p>{final.oneLiner}</p> : null}\n    </>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nSee [Harness Agents](../structured-outputs/harnesses) for the full part list and the repo-report example.\n\n## Typed models & options\n\nLike `openaiCompatible`, you can declare the harness's **models** and its\nper-call **options** so the whole thing is type-checked. `models` constrains the\nfactory's argument; `modelOptions` is a type-only brand (`{} as { … }`, unused at\nruntime) describing what `chat({ modelOptions })` accepts. Declared options are\nmerged with the base ACP options and handed to `command` / `openTransport` as\n`ctx.modelOptions`, so you can turn them into CLI flags:\n\n```ts\nimport { acpCompatible } from '@tanstack/ai-acp'\n\nconst pi = acpCompatible({\n  name: 'pi',\n  models: ['pi-fast', 'pi-pro'],\n  modelOptions: {} as { reasoningEffort?: 'low' | 'high' },\n  command: ({ model, harnessCwd, modelOptions }) =>\n    `pi --acp -m ${model} --cwd ${harnessCwd}` +\n    (modelOptions?.reasoningEffort ? ` --effort ${modelOptions.reasoningEffort}` : ''),\n})\n\npi('pi-pro') // ok\n// pi('pi-ultra') // type error — not in `models`\n```\n\n```ts\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { withSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { pi } from './pi-harness'\nimport { sandbox } from './sandbox'\nimport { messages } from './chat-context'\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: pi('pi-pro'),\n  modelOptions: { reasoningEffort: 'high' }, // typed against the declared options\n  messages,\n  middleware: [withSandbox(sandbox)],\n})\n```\n\nThe base options are always available on `modelOptions` regardless of what you\ndeclare: `sessionId` (resume), `cwd`, `authMode`, `authMethodId`, and\n`permissionMode`.\n\n## Configuration\n\n| Field | Purpose |\n| --- | --- |\n| `name` (required) | Harness label, log prefix, and the `<name>.session-id` CUSTOM event name. |\n| `models` | The model ids this harness accepts — declaring them makes `harness('id')` type-safe (unknown ids are rejected). Omit to accept any string. |\n| `modelOptions` | Type-only brand for the per-call options accepted via `chat({ modelOptions })`. Declare with `{} as { … }`; merged with the base options and exposed on `ctx.modelOptions` in `command` / `openTransport`. |\n| `command` | Build the **stdio** launch command from `{ model, cwd, harnessCwd, sandbox, env, modelOptions, signal }`. Required unless `openTransport` is given. |\n| `skillsDir` | The harness's skills directory (relative to the workspace root, e.g. `'.pi/skills'`) — its native convention, like Claude Code's `.claude/skills`. `withSandbox` workspace `gitSkill`s are linked here. Omit and gitSkills are left unlinked (warned). |\n| `openTransport` | Open any `AcpSessionTransport` yourself (e.g. boot a `serve` process and connect over WebSocket). Overrides `command`. |\n| `cwd` | Working directory inside the sandbox (default `/workspace`). |\n| `env` | Extra environment variables for the harness process. |\n| `authMode` | `'api-key'` (default) uses `authMethodId`. `'host'` skips ACP `authenticate`. See [Harness Auth](../sandbox/auth). |\n| `authMethodId` | ACP auth method to select before the session starts. Ignored when `authMode` is `'host'`. |\n| `permissionMode` | `'default'` \\| `'acceptEdits'` \\| `'bypassPermissions'` (default). |\n| `permissions` | `'headless'` (auto-resolve, default) or `'interactive'` (emit approval-requested events for `ask` prompts). |\n| `onPermissionRequest` | Custom permission handler; overrides `permissions`/`permissionMode`. |\n| `refusalMessage` | `RUN_ERROR` message when the harness refuses a request. |\n| `planEventName` | Emit ACP `plan` updates as a CUSTOM event under this name. |\n| `emitDiff` | Emit the post-run `git diff` of `cwd` as a `file.changed` CUSTOM event (off by default). |\n| `onExtNotification` | Handle vendor `_x/…` JSON-RPC notifications. |\n| `buildPrompt` | Override how chat history maps to the harness prompt. |\n\n## WebSocket and Custom Transports\n\nSome harnesses run an ACP server you reach over WebSocket rather than stdio (the `grok agent serve` pattern). Open the transport yourself with `openTransport` — it receives the same context and returns an `AcpSessionTransport`. Put all teardown in the returned transport's `dispose`:\n\n```ts\nimport { acpCompatible, startAcpServerInSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-acp'\n\nconst myAgent = acpCompatible({\n  name: 'my-agent',\n  openTransport: async ({ sandbox, model, harnessCwd, signal }) => {\n    const server = await startAcpServerInSandbox(sandbox, {\n      port: 9100,\n      cwd: harnessCwd,\n      command: `my-agent serve --bind 0.0.0.0:9100 -m ${model}`,\n      readyMarker: 'listening',\n      buildWsUrl: ({ channel, port }) =>\n        `${channel.url.replace(/^http/i, 'ws')}:${port}`,\n      ...(signal ? { signal } : {}),\n    })\n    const ws = await server.connect(signal)\n    return {\n      kind: 'stream',\n      stream: ws.stream,\n      dispose: async () => {\n        ws.close()\n        await server.dispose()\n      },\n    }\n  },\n})\n```\n\n## Permissions\n\nInside a sandbox the sandbox itself is the security boundary, so the default `'headless'` strategy with `permissionMode: 'bypassPermissions'` lets the agent edit files and run commands without prompting. To surface tool approvals to a client instead, switch to `'interactive'`:\n\n```ts\nimport { acpCompatible } from '@tanstack/ai-acp'\n\nconst pi = acpCompatible({\n  name: 'pi',\n  command: ({ model }) => `pi --acp -m ${model}`,\n  permissions: 'interactive', // emit approval-requested events for `ask` prompts\n  permissionMode: 'acceptEdits', // still auto-approve file edits\n})\n```\n\n`chat()`-provided tools bridged into the agent are always auto-approved, regardless of mode.\n\n## Session Resume\n\nOn every run the adapter emits the harness session id as a CUSTOM event named `<name>.session-id` (e.g. `pi.session-id`). Thread that id back through `modelOptions.sessionId` on the next call and the harness resumes the session — only the trailing user message is sent, since the agent already holds the prior context:\n\n```ts\nimport { chat, chatParamsFromRequest, toServerSentEventsResponse } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { withSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { pi } from './pi-harness' // the configured `acpCompatible(...)` factory\nimport { sandbox } from './sandbox'\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const params = await chatParamsFromRequest(request)\n  const sessionId =\n    typeof params.forwardedProps.sessionId === 'string'\n      ? params.forwardedProps.sessionId\n      : undefined\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: pi('pi-fast'),\n    messages: params.messages,\n    middleware: [withSandbox(sandbox)],\n    modelOptions: { sessionId },\n  })\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}\n```\n\n## Workspace skills\n\nWhen you provision a [workspace](../sandbox/workspace) via `withSandbox`,\n`acpCompatible` projects its skills into the harness — each kind lands where that\nharness expects it:\n\n| Workspace input | How `acpCompatible` projects it |\n| --- | --- |\n| `mcpSkill(name, config)` | Passed to the agent over **ACP natively** via `newSession`'s `mcpServers` (secrets/bearer headers resolved). No config file — that's the ACP advantage over file-based harnesses. |\n| `gitSkill({ repo })` | Cloned during bootstrap, then linked into your declared [`skillsDir`](#configuration) (e.g. `.pi/skills`). Omit `skillsDir` and it's left unlinked (with a warning). |\n| `fileSkill({ path, content })` | Written into the workspace root during bootstrap (provider-agnostic). |\n| `instructions` | Written to `AGENTS.md` (and symlinks) during bootstrap. |\n| `agentSkill(name)`, `plugins` | No generic ACP primitive — warned and skipped. Provide a `gitSkill` or MCP server instead. |\n\n`secrets` declared on the workspace are injected into the agent's environment at\ncreate/resume (never persisted to snapshots), so the harness CLI picks them up\nlike any env var.\n\n## Protocol coverage\n\n`acpCompatible` implements the **client / orchestration** side of ACP — enough to\ndrive an agent through a full prompt turn, not the entire protocol surface. It is\na compliant *minimal* client: everything it doesn't implement is either\ncapability-gated (so advertising non-support is the spec-defined behavior) or a\nrendering choice, never a violation.\n\n**Covered:**\n\n- `initialize` handshake — sends `clientInfo` + the protocol version, negotiates the version, advertises capabilities.\n- `authenticate` (when the agent advertises auth methods), `session/new`, `session/load` (resume), `session/prompt`, `session/cancel`.\n- `session/request_permission` with all four option kinds, mapped by [permission mode](#permissions).\n- All streamed `session/update`s that carry turn output: `agent_message_chunk`, `agent_thought_chunk` (→ reasoning), `tool_call` / `tool_call_update`, `plan`.\n- All five stop reasons (`end_turn`, `max_tokens`, `max_turn_requests`, `refusal`, `cancelled`).\n\n**Surfaced as `CUSTOM` stream events** (the AG-UI chat-event protocol has no\nfirst-class event for non-text assistant output, so these ride on `CUSTOM`):\n\n- `<name>.session-id` — the harness session id, for [resume](#session-resume).\n- `<name>.message-content` — non-text agent content (`image` / `audio` / `resource` / `resource_link` blocks). Its `value` is `{ content: <ACP content block> }`. Non-text **tool** content (diffs, terminal, images) is preserved inside the `TOOL_CALL_RESULT` payload.\n- the plan event, when you set `planEventName`.\n\n**Not implemented (by design):**\n\n- `fs/read_text_file`, `fs/write_text_file`, `terminal/*` — advertised as unsupported. The agent runs inside the sandbox with direct filesystem and shell access, so it never delegates these back to the client.\n- Sending **multimodal prompts** — prompts are sent as text. (Agent multimodal *output* is surfaced via `message-content` above.)\n- Incremental `usage_update` (final turn usage is reported instead), `available_commands_update`, `current_mode_update`, and experimental features (elicitation, NES, providers, session modes/config).\n\n## Next Steps\n\n- [Sandbox Overview](../sandbox/overview) — how harnesses run inside a sandbox\n- [Grok Build Adapter](./grok-build) — a first-class ACP harness adapter\n- [Sandbox Tools](../sandbox/tools) — bridge your app's tools into the agent\n- [OpenAI-Compatible Adapter](./openai-compatible) — the same idea for model providers\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: ACP-Compatible Harness\nid: acp-compatible-harness\ndescription: \"Plug any Agent Client Protocol (ACP) coding agent into a TanStack AI sandbox with one generic harness adapter — no dedicated package required.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - acp\n  - agent client protocol\n  - coding agent\n  - harness\n  - sandbox\n  - custom adapter\n---\n\nCoding-agent CLIs that speak the [Agent Client Protocol](https://agentclientprotocol.com) (ACP) — `grok`, `gemini --acp`, and others — expose a long-lived JSON-RPC session you can drive from a sandbox. Instead of a dedicated package per agent, `acpCompatible` builds a `chat()` adapter for **any** ACP-compliant CLI: configure how to launch it once, select a model per call, and pass it into a sandbox.\n\nIt is the harness equivalent of the [OpenAI-Compatible adapter](./openai-compatible). Use it when your agent speaks ACP but has no `@tanstack/ai-*` package. If a dedicated harness adapter exists ([Grok Build](./grok-build), and others), prefer it — those carry curated per-model metadata and vendor-specific behavior.\n\n## Authentication\n\nThe default `authMode` is `'api-key'`. Set `'host'` when the agent should use\na CLI login on the machine. The sandbox type does not pick this. See\n[Harness Auth](../sandbox/auth).\n\n```ts\nimport { acpCompatibleText } from \"@tanstack/ai-acp\"\n\nacpCompatibleText(\"composer-2.5\", {\n  name: \"acp\",\n  command: ({ model }) => `grok agent -m '${model}' --always-approve stdio`,\n  authMethodId: \"xai.api_key\",\n})\n\nacpCompatibleText(\"composer-2.5\", {\n  name: \"acp\",\n  command: ({ model }) => `grok agent -m '${model}' --always-approve stdio`,\n  authMode: \"host\",\n})\n```\n\n- `'api-key'` (default): call `authenticate` with `authMethodId`.\n- `'host'`: skip ACP `authenticate`. Use the CLI login on the machine.\n\nPass `outputSchema` on the same `chat()` call. `acpCompatible` adds the schema to the prompt and parses the last assistant text. Native harness tools still run on that turn. Read the typed object from `await chat()`, from `useChat().final`, or from the assistant `structured-output` part. See [Harness Agents](../structured-outputs/harnesses).\n\n## Installation\n\n`acpCompatible` ships in `@tanstack/ai-acp`. You drive it inside a sandbox, so install the sandbox package and a provider too:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai-acp @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-sandbox @tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\nvue: @tanstack/ai-acp @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-sandbox @tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\nsolid: @tanstack/ai-acp @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-sandbox @tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai-acp @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-sandbox @tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\npreact: @tanstack/ai-acp @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-sandbox @tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\nangular: @tanstack/ai-acp @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-sandbox @tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai-acp @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-sandbox @tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\noctane: @tanstack/ai-acp @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-sandbox @tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n## Basic Usage\n\nConfigure the harness once with `acpCompatible({ name, command })`, then select a model per call. `command` builds the shell command that launches the agent's ACP server over **stdio** inside the sandbox:\n\n```ts\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { acpCompatible } from '@tanstack/ai-acp'\nimport {\n  createSecrets,\n  defineSandbox,\n  defineWorkspace,\n  githubRepo,\n  withSandbox,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { dockerSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker'\nimport { messages } from './chat-context'\n\n// Configure the \"pi\" agent harness once:\nconst pi = acpCompatible({\n  name: 'pi',\n  command: ({ model, harnessCwd }) => `pi --acp -m ${model} --cwd ${harnessCwd}`,\n  authMethodId: 'pi-api-key', // when the harness advertises an ACP auth method\n  refusalMessage: 'Pi refused the request.',\n})\n\nconst sandbox = defineSandbox({\n  id: 'pi-agent',\n  provider: dockerSandbox({ image: 'node:22' }),\n  workspace: defineWorkspace({\n    source: githubRepo({ repo: 'owner/app' }),\n    setup: ['npm install -g pi-cli'], // install the agent CLI into the image\n    secrets: createSecrets({ PI_API_KEY: process.env.PI_API_KEY ?? '' }),\n  }),\n})\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: pi('pi-fast'),\n  messages,\n  middleware: [withSandbox(sandbox)],\n})\n```\n\nYou get the full ACP flow for free: sandbox resolution, `chat()`-tool → MCP bridging, session resume, permission handling, abort, and AG-UI event translation.\n\n## One-Shot Usage\n\nFor a single model, skip the harness-factory and build the adapter inline with `acpCompatibleText`:\n\n```ts\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { acpCompatibleText } from '@tanstack/ai-acp'\nimport { withSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { sandbox } from './sandbox'\nimport { messages } from './chat-context'\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: acpCompatibleText('pi-fast', {\n    name: 'pi',\n    command: ({ model }) => `pi --acp -m ${model}`,\n  }),\n  messages,\n  middleware: [withSandbox(sandbox)],\n})\n```\n\n## Typed output\n\nPass `outputSchema` on the same `chat()` call. The agent runs its native tools. Then the adapter parses the last assistant text as JSON.\n\n```ts\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { acpCompatibleText } from '@tanstack/ai-acp'\nimport { withSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\nimport { sandbox } from './sandbox'\nimport { messages } from './chat-context'\n\nconst ReportSchema = z.object({\n  name: z.string(),\n  oneLiner: z.string(),\n})\n\nexport async function POST() {\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: acpCompatibleText('pi-fast', {\n      name: 'pi',\n      command: ({ model }) => `pi --acp -m ${model}`,\n    }),\n    messages,\n    outputSchema: ReportSchema,\n    stream: true,\n    middleware: [withSandbox(sandbox)],\n  })\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}\n```\n\nOn the client, walk `messages[].parts` for tool calls and reasoning. Read the typed object from the `structured-output` part or from `useChat().final`.\n\n```tsx\nimport { useChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst ReportSchema = z.object({\n  name: z.string(),\n  oneLiner: z.string(),\n})\n\nfunction Report() {\n  const { messages, final } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/report'),\n    outputSchema: ReportSchema,\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <>\n      {messages.map((message) =>\n        message.parts.map((part, index) => {\n          if (part.type === 'tool-call') {\n            return <p key={part.id}>{part.name}</p>\n          }\n          if (part.type === 'structured-output') {\n            const report = part.data ?? part.partial\n            return report?.name ? <h2 key={index}>{report.name}</h2> : null\n          }\n          return null\n        }),\n      )}\n      {final ? <p>{final.oneLiner}</p> : null}\n    </>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nSee [Harness Agents](../structured-outputs/harnesses) for the full part list and the repo-report example.\n\n## Typed models & options\n\nLike `openaiCompatible`, you can declare the harness's **models** and its\nper-call **options** so the whole thing is type-checked. `models` constrains the\nfactory's argument; `modelOptions` is a type-only brand (`{} as { … }`, unused at\nruntime) describing what `chat({ modelOptions })` accepts. Declared options are\nmerged with the base ACP options and handed to `command` / `openTransport` as\n`ctx.modelOptions`, so you can turn them into CLI flags:\n\n```ts\nimport { acpCompatible } from '@tanstack/ai-acp'\n\nconst pi = acpCompatible({\n  name: 'pi',\n  models: ['pi-fast', 'pi-pro'],\n  modelOptions: {} as { reasoningEffort?: 'low' | 'high' },\n  command: ({ model, harnessCwd, modelOptions }) =>\n    `pi --acp -m ${model} --cwd ${harnessCwd}` +\n    (modelOptions?.reasoningEffort ? ` --effort ${modelOptions.reasoningEffort}` : ''),\n})\n\npi('pi-pro') // ok\n// pi('pi-ultra') // type error — not in `models`\n```\n\n```ts\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { withSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { pi } from './pi-harness'\nimport { sandbox } from './sandbox'\nimport { messages } from './chat-context'\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: pi('pi-pro'),\n  modelOptions: { reasoningEffort: 'high' }, // typed against the declared options\n  messages,\n  middleware: [withSandbox(sandbox)],\n})\n```\n\nThe base options are always available on `modelOptions` regardless of what you\ndeclare: `sessionId` (resume), `cwd`, `authMode`, `authMethodId`, and\n`permissionMode`.\n\n## Configuration\n\n| Field | Purpose |\n| --- | --- |\n| `name` (required) | Harness label, log prefix, and the `<name>.session-id` CUSTOM event name. |\n| `models` | The model ids this harness accepts — declaring them makes `harness('id')` type-safe (unknown ids are rejected). Omit to accept any string. |\n| `modelOptions` | Type-only brand for the per-call options accepted via `chat({ modelOptions })`. Declare with `{} as { … }`; merged with the base options and exposed on `ctx.modelOptions` in `command` / `openTransport`. |\n| `command` | Build the **stdio** launch command from `{ model, cwd, harnessCwd, sandbox, env, modelOptions, signal }`. Required unless `openTransport` is given. |\n| `skillsDir` | The harness's skills directory (relative to the workspace root, e.g. `'.pi/skills'`) — its native convention, like Claude Code's `.claude/skills`. `withSandbox` workspace `gitSkill`s are linked here. Omit and gitSkills are left unlinked (warned). |\n| `openTransport` | Open any `AcpSessionTransport` yourself (e.g. boot a `serve` process and connect over WebSocket). Overrides `command`. |\n| `cwd` | Working directory inside the sandbox (default `/workspace`). |\n| `env` | Extra environment variables for the harness process. |\n| `authMode` | `'api-key'` (default) uses `authMethodId`. `'host'` skips ACP `authenticate`. See [Harness Auth](../sandbox/auth). |\n| `authMethodId` | ACP auth method to select before the session starts. Ignored when `authMode` is `'host'`. |\n| `permissionMode` | `'default'` \\| `'acceptEdits'` \\| `'bypassPermissions'` (default). |\n| `permissions` | `'headless'` (auto-resolve, default) or `'interactive'` (emit approval-requested events for `ask` prompts). |\n| `onPermissionRequest` | Custom permission handler; overrides `permissions`/`permissionMode`. |\n| `refusalMessage` | `RUN_ERROR` message when the harness refuses a request. |\n| `planEventName` | Emit ACP `plan` updates as a CUSTOM event under this name. |\n| `emitDiff` | Emit the post-run `git diff` of `cwd` as a `file.changed` CUSTOM event (off by default). |\n| `onExtNotification` | Handle vendor `_x/…` JSON-RPC notifications. |\n| `buildPrompt` | Override how chat history maps to the harness prompt. |\n\n## WebSocket and Custom Transports\n\nSome harnesses run an ACP server you reach over WebSocket rather than stdio (the `grok agent serve` pattern). Open the transport yourself with `openTransport` — it receives the same context and returns an `AcpSessionTransport`. Put all teardown in the returned transport's `dispose`:\n\n```ts\nimport { acpCompatible, startAcpServerInSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-acp'\n\nconst myAgent = acpCompatible({\n  name: 'my-agent',\n  openTransport: async ({ sandbox, model, harnessCwd, signal }) => {\n    const server = await startAcpServerInSandbox(sandbox, {\n      port: 9100,\n      cwd: harnessCwd,\n      command: `my-agent serve --bind 0.0.0.0:9100 -m ${model}`,\n      readyMarker: 'listening',\n      buildWsUrl: ({ channel, port }) =>\n        `${channel.url.replace(/^http/i, 'ws')}:${port}`,\n      ...(signal ? { signal } : {}),\n    })\n    const ws = await server.connect(signal)\n    return {\n      kind: 'stream',\n      stream: ws.stream,\n      dispose: async () => {\n        ws.close()\n        await server.dispose()\n      },\n    }\n  },\n})\n```\n\n## Permissions\n\nInside a sandbox the sandbox itself is the security boundary, so the default `'headless'` strategy with `permissionMode: 'bypassPermissions'` lets the agent edit files and run commands without prompting. To surface tool approvals to a client instead, switch to `'interactive'`:\n\n```ts\nimport { acpCompatible } from '@tanstack/ai-acp'\n\nconst pi = acpCompatible({\n  name: 'pi',\n  command: ({ model }) => `pi --acp -m ${model}`,\n  permissions: 'interactive', // emit approval-requested events for `ask` prompts\n  permissionMode: 'acceptEdits', // still auto-approve file edits\n})\n```\n\n`chat()`-provided tools bridged into the agent are always auto-approved, regardless of mode.\n\n## Session Resume\n\nOn every run the adapter emits the harness session id as a CUSTOM event named `<name>.session-id` (e.g. `pi.session-id`). Thread that id back through `modelOptions.sessionId` on the next call and the harness resumes the session — only the trailing user message is sent, since the agent already holds the prior context:\n\n```ts\nimport { chat, chatParamsFromRequest, toServerSentEventsResponse } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { withSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { pi } from './pi-harness' // the configured `acpCompatible(...)` factory\nimport { sandbox } from './sandbox'\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const params = await chatParamsFromRequest(request)\n  const sessionId =\n    typeof params.forwardedProps.sessionId === 'string'\n      ? params.forwardedProps.sessionId\n      : undefined\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: pi('pi-fast'),\n    messages: params.messages,\n    middleware: [withSandbox(sandbox)],\n    modelOptions: { sessionId },\n  })\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}\n```\n\n## Workspace skills\n\nWhen you provision a [workspace](../sandbox/workspace) via `withSandbox`,\n`acpCompatible` projects its skills into the harness — each kind lands where that\nharness expects it:\n\n| Workspace input | How `acpCompatible` projects it |\n| --- | --- |\n| `mcpSkill(name, config)` | Passed to the agent over **ACP natively** via `newSession`'s `mcpServers` (secrets/bearer headers resolved). No config file — that's the ACP advantage over file-based harnesses. |\n| `gitSkill({ repo })` | Cloned during bootstrap, then linked into your declared [`skillsDir`](#configuration) (e.g. `.pi/skills`). Omit `skillsDir` and it's left unlinked (with a warning). |\n| `fileSkill({ path, content })` | Written into the workspace root during bootstrap (provider-agnostic). |\n| `instructions` | Written to `AGENTS.md` (and symlinks) during bootstrap. |\n| `agentSkill(name)`, `plugins` | No generic ACP primitive — warned and skipped. Provide a `gitSkill` or MCP server instead. |\n\n`secrets` declared on the workspace are injected into the agent's environment at\ncreate/resume (never persisted to snapshots), so the harness CLI picks them up\nlike any env var.\n\n## Protocol coverage\n\n`acpCompatible` implements the **client / orchestration** side of ACP — enough to\ndrive an agent through a full prompt turn, not the entire protocol surface. It is\na compliant *minimal* client: everything it doesn't implement is either\ncapability-gated (so advertising non-support is the spec-defined behavior) or a\nrendering choice, never a violation.\n\n**Covered:**\n\n- `initialize` handshake — sends `clientInfo` + the protocol version, negotiates the version, advertises capabilities.\n- `authenticate` (when the agent advertises auth methods), `session/new`, `session/load` (resume), `session/prompt`, `session/cancel`.\n- `session/request_permission` with all four option kinds, mapped by [permission mode](#permissions).\n- All streamed `session/update`s that carry turn output: `agent_message_chunk`, `agent_thought_chunk` (→ reasoning), `tool_call` / `tool_call_update`, `plan`.\n- All five stop reasons (`end_turn`, `max_tokens`, `max_turn_requests`, `refusal`, `cancelled`).\n\n**Surfaced as `CUSTOM` stream events** (the AG-UI chat-event protocol has no\nfirst-class event for non-text assistant output, so these ride on `CUSTOM`):\n\n- `<name>.session-id` — the harness session id, for [resume](#session-resume).\n- `<name>.message-content` — non-text agent content (`image` / `audio` / `resource` / `resource_link` blocks). Its `value` is `{ content: <ACP content block> }`. Non-text **tool** content (diffs, terminal, images) is preserved inside the `TOOL_CALL_RESULT` payload.\n- the plan event, when you set `planEventName`.\n\n**Not implemented (by design):**\n\n- `fs/read_text_file`, `fs/write_text_file`, `terminal/*` — advertised as unsupported. The agent runs inside the sandbox with direct filesystem and shell access, so it never delegates these back to the client.\n- Sending **multimodal prompts** — prompts are sent as text. (Agent multimodal *output* is surfaced via `message-content` above.)\n- Incremental `usage_update` (final turn usage is reported instead), `available_commands_update`, `current_mode_update`, and experimental features (elicitation, NES, providers, session modes/config).\n\n## Next Steps\n\n- [Sandbox Overview](../sandbox/overview) — how harnesses run inside a sandbox\n- [Grok Build Adapter](./grok-build) — a first-class ACP harness adapter\n- [Sandbox Tools](../sandbox/tools) — bridge your app's tools into the agent\n- [OpenAI-Compatible Adapter](./openai-compatible) — the same idea for model providers\n"}
